### Version history (Git-backed)
### Routes: /api/versions/*
###
### Every save is committed to Git, so documents have a version history addressed by
### commit hash. All endpoints take the document `path` as a query parameter.

@docPath = /getting-started

### List versions of a document (newest first)
# @name versions
GET {{apiUrl}}/versions?path={{docPath}}
# => 200 { "path": ..., "versions": [ { "hash": "...", ... } ], "total": n }

### Get a document as it was at a specific commit
GET {{apiUrl}}/versions/document?path={{docPath}}&hash=REPLACE_WITH_COMMIT_HASH
# => 200 { "path": ..., "hash": ..., "document": {...} }

### Diff a document between two commits
GET {{apiUrl}}/versions/diff?path={{docPath}}&hash1=REPLACE_WITH_OLD_HASH&hash2=REPLACE_WITH_NEW_HASH
# => 200 { "diff": "..." }

### Restore a document to a previous version (params go in the query string, not a body)
POST {{apiUrl}}/versions/restore?path={{docPath}}&hash=REPLACE_WITH_COMMIT_HASH
# => 200 { "message": "Document restored successfully", "path": ..., "hash": ... }

#############################################
### Error cases
#############################################

### Missing required path parameter
GET {{apiUrl}}/versions

### Missing hash parameter
GET {{apiUrl}}/versions/document?path={{docPath}}
